cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "pm-dem-sm: Polyhedral-Based DEM Surrogate Modeling for Time Series Prediction in Bidisperse Particle Mixing and Segregation"
abstract: >-
  Terminal project of the UNISON MCD academic program. A YADE-based
  polyhedral DEM simulation pipeline for bidisperse particle mixing and
  segregation in a rotating mill, and an extended-RNNSR surrogate (GRU plus a
  stochastic-random model) for time-series prediction of the particle frames,
  with mixing/segregation metrics and visualization tools.
authors:
  - given-names: Fernando
    family-names: Martinez
    affiliation: "Universidad de Sonora"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LFer-MM/pm-dem-sm"
license: MIT
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-21"
keywords:
  - discrete element method
  - DEM
  - YADE
  - polyhedral particles
  - surrogate modeling
  - recurrent neural network
  - granular mixing
  - segregation
